{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>הלא</b> And by way of metaphor, like the proverb: they will lift up riddles for him, which are hidden." "<b>הוי המרבה לא לו</b> This is to seize dwellings — not his." "Yefet said: for the meaning is וּמַכְבִּיד עָלָיו, like a madman who throws mud upon himself. And the Nagid said: that he adds to build a dwelling and does not save it, and the word עֲבַטִּיט comes in the manner of all plurals of peoples."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {2 "הנגיד resolved as 'the Nagid,' likely referring to Samuel ibn Naghrilla; עבטיט appears to be a grammatical form under discussion; the argument is compressed and obscure, rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:05.697705122Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}